-- title:
--   Change of presentation for corners of the Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $M \geq 1$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals and $S_0$ a finite set of naturals containing no prime divisor of $M$, and assume that for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ one has $\ell \in S_0$ if and only if $\ell \in S$. Write $H^1 = H^1(M,\top,\mathcal{O})$ for the $\mathcal{O}$-module of additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_H(M)$ with $H = \top$ (that is, $\Gamma_0(M)$) to $\mathcal{O}$, and let [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) attach to each generator in [`CohCarrier.Gen M S₀`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) — the symbols $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S_0$, $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, and $\langle d\rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ — an $\mathcal{O}$-endomorphism of $H^1$; assume, as `hcomm`, that these operators for $S_0$ commute pairwise. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative module-finite $\mathcal{O}$-algebra acting on $H^1$ compatibly with the $\mathcal{O}$-action, let $Sp$ be an `IdempotentSplitting` of $\mathbb{T}$ (a complete family of orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_j$ exhausting the maximal spectrum, with $e_j \in \mathfrak{m}_{j'}$ exactly for $j \neq j'$), and fix an index $i$ such that the corner submodule $e_i H^1$ is finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$. Suppose further given $t \colon$ `Gen M S` $\to \mathbb{T}$ and $c \colon$ `Gen M S` $\to \mathcal{O}$ with: every element of $\mathbb{T}$ acting on $H^1$ as some element of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1)$ generated by the operators indexed by `Gen M S`; $t(g)$ acting as the operator attached to $g$; $t(g) - c(g) \in \mathfrak{m}_i$; every $v \in H^1$ on which all $t(g) - c(g)$ act topologically nilpotently (for each $k$ some power carries $v$ into $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^k H^1$) lying in $e_i H^1$; $c(\langle d\rangle) \equiv 1$ modulo the maximal ideal; $e_i H^1 \neq 0$; and the corner ring $e_i \mathbb{T} e_i$ acting faithfully on $e_i H^1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a map $\bar\theta \colon$ `Gen M S₀` $\to$ `ResidueField 𝒪` with $\bar\theta(T_\ell)$ and $\bar\theta(U_q)$ the residues of the corresponding values of $c$ (the $T$-generators matched through the hypothesis relating $S_0$ and $S$) and $\bar\theta(\langle d\rangle) = 1$, an `IdempotentSplitting` $Sp'$ of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1)$ generated by the operators indexed by `Gen M S₀` (the `opSubalgebra` of the `HeckeData` built from `opFamily`, `hcomm` and $\bar\theta$), an index $i_0$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\pi$ from the corner ring of $Sp'$ at $i_0$ to the residue field sending the corner image of each generating operator $g$ to $\bar\theta(g)$, and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra isomorphism $e_B$ from $e_i\mathbb{T}e_i$ to that corner ring, such that the two corner submodules of $H^1$ have the same elements, $e_B$ carries the corner image of $t(T_\ell)$ and of $t(U_q)$ to the corner image of the operator $T_\ell$ respectively $U_q$, and $e_B$ is equivariant: for $x$ in $e_i\mathbb{T}e_i$ and elements of the two corner submodules with equal underlying value in $H^1$, the values of $x \cdot m$ and $e_B(x) \cdot m'$ in $H^1$ agree.
--
--   This is the change-of-presentation lemma identifying an abstractly presented local factor of a Hecke algebra acting on $H^1(\Gamma_0(M),\mathcal{O})$ with a corner of the algebra concretely generated by the operators $T_\ell$, $U_q$ and $\langle d\rangle$ on that cohomology, matching corner modules, corner rings and generators. It feeds the $\Sigma$-corner identification and rank results at level $\Gamma_0(M)$, being cited by [`CohCarrier.free_sigmaCorner_gammaZero`](thm.html#CohCarrier.free_sigmaCorner_gammaZero), [`CohCarrier.torsionBySet_ne_bot_and_finrank_sigmaCornerSubmodule_auxLevel_eq_mul`](thm.html#CohCarrier.torsionBySet_ne_bot_and_finrank_sigmaCornerSubmodule_auxLevel_eq_mul) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel).
